oad_count":33,"created_at":"2026-10-24T00:56:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T00:56:54Z"},{"id":670873297,"node_id":"RA_kwDOPYoUTM4n_LbR","name":"openspec-windows-x64.exe","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":98526208,"digest":"sha256:dcccc028b89c4a3b0c80ee52c454c6dee98af994e6caa55302ae69f880559d68","download_count":1322,"created_at":"2026-10-24T00:56:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T00:56:54Z"},{"id":670873423,"node_id":"RA_kwDOPYoUTM4n_LdP","name":"SHA256SUMS","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":712,"digest":"sha256:0bab318c42d84f2e1fad378d0c55f54ef24f7f64a24551992c0718f5e9f532d0","download_count":3341,"created_at":"2026-10-24T00:56:55Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T00:56:56Z"}],"body":"## What's New in v1.15.0\r\n\r\nYou can now install OpenSpec without Node.js, using one command, and `openspec update` can now show what it would change before changing anything.\r\n\r\n### New\r\n\r\n- **Standalone install** - Install OpenSpec with one command and no Node.js: `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec/main/scripts/binary/install.sh | sh` on macOS and Linux, or `irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec/main/scripts/binary/install.ps1 | iex` on Windows. Every release now ships binaries for macOS, Linux (glibc and musl) and Windows on x64 and arm64, with `SHA256SUMS`. npm and the other package managers keep working as before.\r\n- **`openspec update --dry-run`** - Reports the files an update would add, change or delete without writing anything; add `--json` for machine-readable output.\r\n\r\n### Improved\r\n\r\n- **Faster `--json` commands** - `status`, `instructions`, `new change`, `templates`, `validate` and `schema` no longer load the spinner package when run with `--json`, so they start a little faster. Output is unchanged.\r\n- **`openspec feedback`** - Filed issues now match the bug form, and the manual-submission link opens the bug form with your message, version and environment filled in.\r\n\r\n### Fixed\r\n\r\n- **`openspec new change`** - The progress line now names the schema the change is actually created with, instead of always saying `spec-driven`.\r\n- **`/opsx:verify`** - A REMOVED requirement is matched to its baseline by its exact name, so a similarly named replacement is no longer mistaken for it.\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec/compare/v1.14.3...v1.15.0\r\n","reactions":{"total_count":8,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":8,"eyes":0}}
